* {{rhymes|en|ɪljən|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|mathematics}} Of an algebraic structure (usually a [[group]] or [[algebra]]), having a [[commutative]] defining operation. {{defdate|Mid 19<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref>{{R:SOED5|page=3}}</ref>
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1996|author=Barry Simon|title=Representations of Finite and Compact Groups|page=50|passage=The interesting aspect here is that U<sub>3</sub> is [[irreducible]], even though all [[irrep]]s over the [[complex]]es are one-dimensional because ℤ<sub>4</sub> is [[abelian]].}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} Of a binary function, [[commutative]].

